  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Collections\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Collections\n       Program: commons-collections\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/Collections.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-collections.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 28\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Collections-8\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n7cf943172b154019d7c6a66f4290272b2144e29a\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2008-03-16 00:26:44 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCOLLECTIONS-220\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/COLLECTIONS-220\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.buffer.TestUnboundedFifoBuffer::testCollections220\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: expected:<1> but was:<0>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.buffer.UnboundedFifoBuffer\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Serialization/Deserialization doesn't work well with empty buffers.\nType: Bug | Priority: Minor | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nWhen I serialize the queue to disk an it has elements, all works ok, but when I serialize an empty queue I have some problems when I create a new object using the serialized file.\n\nWhen I deserialize the queue it has a 'buffer' with size 1 (with null content), 'tail' and 'head' fields are 0 (they are declared transient). So, when I try to add a new object to the queue, the sentence:\n\n Object[] tmp = new Object[((buffer.length - 1) * 2) + 1];\n\nIs executed in the add() method to increase the buffer length, but the buffer remains with the same size! (buffer.length = 1 --> (1 - 1) * 2 + 1 = 1). So, the object is added and when the tail is going to be incremented, it is reset to 0!! \n\n    private int increment(int index) {\n        index++;\n        if (index >= buffer.length) {\n            index = 0;\n        }\n        return index;\n    }\n\n\nSo it is impossible to add new elements after an empty queue has been serialized / deserialized.\n\nI attach a simple TestCase where this is proved. The example works when you use XMLEncoder to serialize the buffer but doesn't work if you use ObjectOutputStream or XStream.\n\nComments:\n\n[Dave Meikle]: Proposed Patch to fix Object Serialization Problem\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Nice simple patch. +1.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Attaching a unit test for this, along with Dave's previously attached fix.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: svn ci -m \"Applying a unit test for COLLECTIONS-220. AbstractTestObject is refactored to provide a utility method that serializes and then deserializes. Dave Meikle's fix for said unit test is also applied. \" src\n\nSending        src/java/org/apache/commons/collections/buffer/UnboundedFifoBuffer.java\nSending        src/test/org/apache/commons/collections/AbstractTestObject.java\nSending        src/test/org/apache/commons/collections/buffer/TestUnboundedFifoBuffer.java\nTransmitting file data ...\nCommitted revision 637495.\n\n[Thomas Neidhart]: The Buffer interface/implementations have been removed, thus this fix is obsolete.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.collections.buffer.UnboundedFifoBuffer (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.collections.buffer.UnboundedFifoBuffer (fixed)\n@@ -115,6 +115,7 @@\n     private void writeObject(ObjectOutputStream out) throws IOException {\n         out.defaultWriteObject();\n         out.writeInt(size());\n+        out.writeInt(buffer.length);\n         for (Iterator it = iterator(); it.hasNext();) {\n             out.writeObject(it.next());\n         }\n@@ -130,7 +131,8 @@\n     private void readObject(ObjectInputStream in) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {\n         in.defaultReadObject();\n         int size = in.readInt();\n-        buffer = new Object[size + 1];\n+        int length = in.readInt();\n+        buffer = new Object[length];\n         for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n             buffer[i] = in.readObject();\n         }"
}